Z||000000||CUTTER||04-20-2000||01:15 AM||||I just got a used transmition for my 87GT out of a 1984 pontiac 6000, It runs great but my one friends "seams" to know alot about cars and said that the tranny wont last because its from a differnt car! I do drive the car fast at times. The tranny shifts good Im just worried that it wont last. I dont think the prev. owner beat it or anything, I have no-clue how many miles are on it. My garage did it for me for $450. And got the tranny out of there junk-yard. If I dont beat the tranny should it last? <P>Another question.... when Im racing or driving fast... SOMETIMES my gas peddel gets a little harder to push down, you have to press almost 3 times as hard to get it to the floor, almost like some kind of restriction holding it back. Then when this happens, If I slam the gas the tranny will shift earlier then usual and im watching the tach, it shifts about 4000 and the needle goes down 3 times slower then normal. But when I turn the car off for a while and startdriving it again its fine. It did it about 3-4 times so far in the last 2 months. 2 months ago is when I got my tranny put in...uh oh. hope its not the tranny. could it be a fuel pump/filter or something like that?<P>One more question... my whole steering wheel and colume are loose about 1/2" of give on the whole thing, It doesnt effect the steering at all just people say I should get it fixed and it could be exspensive. What is wrong with it and around how much will it cost?<BR>  Sorry this post is so long, Thanks alot, Shane||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-20-2000||01:31 AM||||I wouldn't worry about the transmission.  Both are TH125 models and I've heard from more than one source that there's no difference in durability through the years. The only thing that may be different is the torque converter, but I'm not sure on that. Just make sure your fluid is pink and doesn't smell like toast!  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||CUTTER||04-20-2000||03:57 AM||||Yeah its pink, could it be the fuel pump or filter?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||04-20-2000||11:05 AM||||Sounds like you might have a bind in your throttle cable or something. You should be able to yank a whole steering column assy out of another car, maybe even the car that gave up the tranny?, and get back in business for much less than it would cost to rebuild steering column.<P>The tranny wont go bad just because its from another car.  Chances are your Ok<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-20-2000||11:27 AM||||The throttle cable or the cable from the TBI to the tranny is binding. Get it fixed.<P>Your friend doesn't know much. Doesn't matter what car it came from. TH125 is TH125. For the most part. I would have tried to find a newer one. The TH125's were improved considerably over the years.<P>The top part of the steering column needs some fairly major work done. Esier to replace it. follow the Ogre CAve link at the bottom of this page and read it before any steering column work.||||reg||1
